<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    kuna vexzeroupper: P2 flow, option vexzeroupper (default on).

      0x1000 addi: vpaddd ymm0,ymm0,ymm1; ret
      0x1010 fma3: vfmadd132ps ymm0,ymm2,ymm1; ret
      0x1020 scal: vmulsd xmm0,xmm0,[rdi]; vmovsd [rdi],xmm0; vmovsd xmm0,[rdi]; ret

    The SLEIGH spec writes the result of a VEX instruction as one zero-extended
    write of all of ZMM0, so heritage widens the ymm0 the instruction reads to
    64 bytes and the read comes back as SUB6432(zmm0,0).

    Asserts #1-#2 are the off pass: a 64-byte local, truncated at each use.
    Asserts #3-#4 are the on pass: ymm0 is read at its own 32 bytes.
    Assert #5 is the on pass over scal: the scalar product is split too, so the
    reloaded xmm0 is the returned double (a whole-ZMM scalar write left the
    function void).
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x1000" readonly="true">c5fdfec1c3</bytechunk>
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x1010" readonly="true">c4e26d98c1c3</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x1000" name="addi"/>
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x1020" readonly="true">c5fb5907c5fb1107c5fb1007c3</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x1010" name="fma3"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x1020" name="scal"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>option vexzeroupper off</com>
  <com>lo fu addi</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu fma3</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option vexzeroupper on</com>
  <com>lo fu addi</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu fma3</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu scal</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="vexzeroupper #1: off, ymm0 is a 64-byte local in both functions and in neither with the option on" min="2" max="2">char \w+ \[64\];</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="vexzeroupper #2: off, each read of ymm0 truncates the widened register" min="2" max="2">SUB6432\(\w+,0\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="vexzeroupper #3: on, the add reads ymm0 whole" min="1" max="1">_mm256_add_epi32\(v1,v2\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="vexzeroupper #4: on, the FMA reads ymm0 whole" min="1" max="1">_mm256_fmadd_ps\(v1,v2,v3\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="vexzeroupper #5: on, a scalar product stored, reloaded and returned is a double result" min="1" max="1">float8 scal\(float8 a0,float8 \*a1\)</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
